# Merge attributes (#1112). `merge=union` keeps both sides of a conflicting
# hunk with no markers. It suits append-only edits only: two PRs that each add
# a line or a section at the same place, such as two M25 campaign scenarios.
# A reorder or rewrite of existing text can merge into duplicated or garbled
# text with no conflict to flag it, so such a change still needs a normal
# review of the merged result.
# GitHub's server-side mergeability check is not documented to honour these
# attributes: a PR may still show as conflicting there. The builder's local
# merge-up (`git merge main`) then applies the union with no manual edit.
# scripts/check-repo.py (`attributes`) fails if a line below goes missing.
docs/campaign-harness.md merge=union
